News
====

The main functional changes in the 2.7 release are to fix the address verifier
exit-100 bug, allow the "--port" option to be used more than once, add a new
"--poll-run" option, and set better file permissions when delivering to a
maildir mailbox.

Scripts for doing Windows builds and for generating documentation have been
reworked, with a shift towards cmake, Qt6, MbedTLS v3 and sphinx, and away from
doxygen.

The documentation files are de-duplicated by standardising on the CommonMark
format. These files can be processed by "pandoc" using its "-raw_html" and
"-smart" options and by sphinx by using the MyST-Parser.

Building for Windows using v3 of MbedTLS with TLS1.3 support can now be the
default since the v2/v3 regression with respect to client verification of server
certificates when using TLS1.3 has finally been resolved. However, using v3 for
the Windows XP build requires some customisation to revert to using CryptoAPI
rather than CNG (bcrypt).

The G_LIB_SMALL optimisation is withdrawn since the same code-size benefits can
be realised using compiler/linker options. These can be conveniently activated
by passing "-z" to the "configure.sh" wrapper script. (For even smaller binaries
use "make -C unity small", as before.)

Alpine Linux packages can now be created with "make apk". This has triggered a
rework of the autoconf "make install" logic so that the template config file,
pam file, auth file, systemd unit file and sysv-init scripts are all installed
as example files by default. The config file is additionally installed under
/etc and the pam file is additionally installed to /etc/pam.d (e_pamdir) using
no-clobber copies that can be disabled with "--disable-install-config"
(previously "--disable-install-hook") and "--disable-install-pam" respectively.
The sysv-init script is installed to /etc/init.d only if "e_initdir" is defined
appropriately, and similarly, the systemd unit file is only installed under
/usr/lib/systemd only if "e_systemddir" is so defined.
